<%# Simple Interest result (spec issue #78, DESIGN.md §4 Hero-result + Stat grid). The
    ending balance (total) is the headline answer — a big tabular-nums figure on the coral-
    ruled hero card — with the interest accrued read into the detail sentence beside the
    principal/rate/term it came from. Below, the principal → interest → total breakdown is a
    RESPONSIVE AUTO-FIT STAT GRID (DESIGN.md §4 "Stat grid"): three label-over-value cards
    sized to a min width and left to wrap/flow (≈3-across on a wide panel, collapsing as it
    narrows), tabular-nums so the money columns align and never clip even at 6+ digits.
    Interest is the positive/derived figure, so it reads in accent green (DESIGN.md §1).
    `calc:` is a valid Calculators::SimpleInterest; result keys are `interest` + `total`
    (ARCHITECTURE.md §4). %>
<% interest = calc.result[:interest] %>
<% total = calc.result[:total] %>
<% unit_label = calc.unit == "months" ? "months" : "years" %>
<div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
  <div class="flex gap-5 p-7">
    <span class="w-[5px] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Ending balance</p>
      <p class="mt-2 flex items-baseline gap-1.5">
        <span class="text-sm font-bold text-faint">$</span>
        <span class="text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.04em] tabular-nums text-ink"><%= money_display(total) %></span>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <span class="font-semibold text-accent">$<%= money_display(interest) %></span>
        in simple interest on a $<%= money_display(calc.principal) %> principal at
        <%= decimal_display(calc.rate) %>% over <%= decimal_display(calc.time) %> <%= unit_label %>.
      </p>

      <%# Breakdown — a responsive auto-fit stat grid (DESIGN.md §4 "Stat grid"): the cards
          size to a min width and flow, so the same panel reads 3-across when wide and
          wraps/stacks as it narrows, never pinning a fixed column count. The arbitrary
          grid-template-columns is justified per DESIGN.md §5 (the standard scale can't
          express auto-fit). The min width is 11rem — wide enough that a 6+ digit money
          figure ($1,800,000.00) fits one card without truncation, and so the grid drops to
          fewer columns (giving each card more room) on a narrower panel before any value can
          clip (DESIGN.md §4 "must never clip"). text-xl + tabular-nums + break-words keeps
          the figure whole at large magnitudes. Interest is the derived/positive figure →
          accent green (DESIGN.md §1); principal + total read in ink. %>
      <dl class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(11rem,1fr))] gap-3">
        <div class="rounded-[13px] border border-border bg-bg/60 p-4">
          <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Principal</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1.5 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-ink break-words">$<%= money_display(calc.principal) %></dd>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-[13px] border border-border bg-bg/60 p-4">
          <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Interest</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1.5 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-accent break-words">+&nbsp;$<%= money_display(interest) %></dd>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-[13px] border border-border bg-bg/60 p-4">
          <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Total</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1.5 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-ink break-words">$<%= money_display(total) %></dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
